# nl-backend-turn-1: provider tuning variables and Office text in read. Written without compiling (no cargo run in this wave).

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/Cargo.toml `[dev-dependencies]`, after the line `tempfile = { workspace = true }`:
mixdog-ooxml-text = { workspace = true }
# Needs nr-exthost-ooxml-text.wire applied first (member + [workspace.dependencies] row for mixdog-ooxml-text); the edge is
# test-only (fs/read.rs `office_text_tests` answers `ooxml.text` with the real extractor over a stored .docx and .xlsx).
# Cargo.lock: `cargo update --workspace --offline` adds the edge; mixdog-workspace-hack needs nothing.

## 2. Nothing else
# No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no compose_flip change. MIXDOG_PROVIDER_RETRY_JITTER_RATIO is read through the existing
# `FirstByteSettings::process()` snapshot (providers/first_byte.rs), so crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/tests/credential_source_scan_tests.rs
# needs no new ALLOWED row (no new direct environment read was added).
